WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.100
Here we are at Lazar's Canyon and Lazar's Cave.

2
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:43.000
We came here to go into the cave, but we'll have to leave that for another time,

3
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.820
because we didn't find out the opening hours very well.

4
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:59.000
You can't come here on your own: on weekdays an organized tour of 20 people is required.

5
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:06.000
Some days are non-working, later I'll show you the exact hours, I didn't memorize them well,

6
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.260
but on weekends you can come on your own.

7
00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.420
There's a restaurant nearby: you cross the river, and there's the restaurant.

8
00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:18.180
They serve trout, of course.

9
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.840
And as for Lazar's Canyon itself, it's the longest canyon in Serbia.

10
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:29.820
The place is wonderful, the forest is really dense,

11
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.440
and, of course, there are various species of plants and animals here,

12
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:43.880
which are protected and which you have to be careful with, because there are bears, wildcats and so on.

13
00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:53.370
This is the entrance to the cave itself, and here are the opening hours, I'll film them for you now.

14
00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:59.550
You need to wear a mask, gloves. See: Monday closed, Tuesday closed,

15
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.130
Wednesday, Thursday, Friday — only for groups registered in advance.

16
00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:22.830
There's a phone number here, you can call if you want to go, a ticket is 200 dinars.

17
00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.690
I have around 2200 points left on my Smile card.

18
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.710
I don't know if I've told you about the Smile card, I think not.

19
00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:59.330
I don't know when the Smile program started, a few years ago already,

20
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:05.770
I used to have a plastic one, you know, like a payment card, and now it's an app.

21
00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.910
Every time you buy something at a gas station, fuel or anything in the store,

22
00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.190
you swipe the Smile card and collect points.

23
00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.110
There's a catalog, you can take one at any gas station, and it's also in the app once you download it.

24
00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.810
In the catalog you can see how many points each item costs,

25
00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:23.430
when you've collected the needed number of points for the item you want,

26
00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.990
you go, scan your code, they give you the item, the points are deducted — and that's it.

27
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:34.670
I don't know what we haven't taken: pots, saucepans, chargers, I mean for the car, there's nothing I haven't taken.

28
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.650
A travel toy, maybe a travel toy.

29
00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:59.310
As I said, I collected exactly as many points as needed for this toy for Nadja.

30
00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:05.150
It's like a travel pillow, literally, and it says: I'm your new friend, Lily the lamb.

31
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:07.990
And a vacuum cleaner for the car.

32
00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.070
Yes, her name is Lily.

33
00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:34.990
A new toy.

34
00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:35.790
Okay, are we done?

35
00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:38.030
Let's go, come on.

36
00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.530
They brought us dinner.

37
00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:45.210
One pljeskavica, one white meat.

38
00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.950
The portions are clearly huge, and these are the small ones, by the way.

39
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:54.070
Besides the pljeskavica, there are also these flatbreads and salad.

40
00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:04.410
The room is lovely, but I'll film it for you better tomorrow, because we're really too tired now.

41
00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:20.500
Nothing worked out with Lazar's Cave.

42
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:27.100
So we decided to come to the Resava Cave, it's not too far from our lodging, about half an hour.

43
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:33.840
And we found it very easily.

44
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.700
During the tour you have to wear masks, and there's a big crowd here.

45
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.120
But you can hear that there are people.

46
00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:49.000
So I'll see what's inside and whether it's worth coming.

47
00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:57.800
So we'll see.

48
00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.000
And here I am in the cave.

49
00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.700
I don't know how well you can hear me.

50
00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.260
So you should bring some jacket with you.

51
00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.440
You can also rent jackets here,

52
00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:15.680
if you didn't bring one.

53
00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:19.460
The route through the cave is about 800 meters.

54
00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:25.020
I don't know whether I managed to record it when the guide was talking.

55
00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.620
So now we're moving on.

56
00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:28.740
We're going to some concert hall.

57
00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.680
The cave really is beautiful.

58
00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.420
And it's huge.

59
00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.400
What I must tell you is that

60
00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.180
you must not touch

61
00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.320
anything at all.

62
00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.680
Except these railings, if you need to hold on.

63
00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:08.860
And that's it.

64
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.820
I hope you can hear me.

65
00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:28.400
And this is the concert hall.

66
00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.360
It's crazy how it looks.

67
00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:34.380
Beautiful.

68
00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.420
I really filmed a lot of shots for you.

69
00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.740
But come and see it, because it's really interesting.

70
00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:58.840
Slowly leaving the cave.

71
00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:03.660
Good Lord.

72
00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.800
I'm going to look for Saša and the little one.

73
00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.940
And then we're driving to the waterfall,

74
00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.440
so I can warm up a bit.

75
00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.480
Sneakers are a must here,

76
00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.600
because it's very muddy.

77
00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.260
It's seven degrees here,

78
00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.180
so it's cool.

79
00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:23.940
Nothing dangerous.

80
00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.380
I don't recommend it for children.

81
00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.560
I mean, very small children.

82
00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.080
Well, where are my two little ones?

83
00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.400
Here we are.

84
00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:35.900
We ate.

85
00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:37.740
Let's go.

86
00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.000
We slept a little.

87
00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:40.360
You slept?

88
00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.550
You have to walk from where you leave the car to the waterfall.

89
00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:15.630
By the way, a very beautiful road,

90
00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.230
more precisely this path we're walking along.

91
00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:20.290
And climbing over the fence is prohibited.

92
00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.300
I hope you can see and hear me well.

93
00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.060
And it's very important to me that under these videos you write in the comments how well you can hear and see us,

94
00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.520
because I'm testing new equipment,

95
00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.000
and it's very important for me to know.

96
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:37.580
Thank you.

97
00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:46.970
I'll film it for you now.

98
00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:49.070
The crowd is huge.

99
00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.960
And we saw the waterfall

100
00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:57.660
Veliki Buk.

101
00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:58.860
It's very cold down below.

102
00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.500
The wind blows

103
00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.660
and sprays water.

104
00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:04.320
Nadja is dressed very warmly.

105
00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:08.880
Fully, as if it were winter.

106
00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.780
But she saw the waterfall too.

107
00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.860
They say the steps are a bit problematic.

108
00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.460
We've sort of gotten used to it, so it's not too hard for me.

109
00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:23.260
It's probably a bit hard for Saša,

110
00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:28.280
because he has a double load after all.

111
00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:33.300
People were whining on the way up.

112
00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:33.980
Funny.

113
00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.900
Yes, nothing special.

114
00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.040
Of course, littering is prohibited here, pitching tents is prohibited.

115
00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:52.200
I want to say, I keep repeating this so people get used to it and learn not to litter, not to light fires and all that.

116
00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:55.960
We're now going to see what to have for dinner.

117
00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:59.100
And, basically, that's all for today.

118
00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.080
Tomorrow — a new direction, a new place.

119
00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.180
And here we didn't want to linger

120
00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.140
because of the crowd.

121
00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.520
There really are a lot of people here.

122
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.840
We hid in one corner.

123
00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:16.360
And, basically, that's all.

124
00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:32.460
The "Lisinski raj" restaurant

125
00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.200
we're leaving behind, because

126
00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:36.500
they don't accept cards there.

127
00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.740
Wonderful setting,

128
00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:41.140
they say the food is very tasty,

129
00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:42.940
and the most interesting thing —

130
00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.000
it's located

131
00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.340
in the rock.

132
00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:46.700
That is, there are three tables,

133
00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:50.120
and you can have dinner in the rock.

134
00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:51.720
But since,

135
00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:53.800
unfortunately, they don't accept cards,

136
00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.060
we'll have to find another place

137
00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.360
to eat, but look:

138
00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.820
the setting is

139
00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:01.460
simply wonderful.

140
00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.940
They thought of literally everything.

141
00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:06.660
The road to the restaurant itself is excellent,

142
00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.620
parking is literally in front of the entrance,

143
00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.720
but you have to walk a little up the steps

144
00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:11.080
up and down.

145
00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.740
Since dinner didn't work out so far,

146
00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.120
we're rushing to the lodging,

147
00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.080
because our lodging is a bit

148
00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.580
far from town,

149
00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:20.980
and you have to get to it

150
00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:22.220
by a dirt road,

151
00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:23.960
so

152
00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.720
it wasn't very nice for us

153
00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.180
yesterday, when we drove

154
00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.140
at night,

155
00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:29.260
so now we want to arrive

156
00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:30.740
a bit earlier.

157
00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.840
You know that I,

158
00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:43.480
I said it at some point,

159
00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:44.560
forgot my T-shirts,

160
00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:52.260
and I'm forced to wear these bodysuits

161
00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:52.900
from "Zara."

162
00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.700
It's simply horrible synthetic stuff.

163
00:12:56.780 --> 00:13:01.380
Literally, I think my whole skin became inflamed.

164
00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.260
I can't wait until

165
00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.060
I take this off,

166
00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:05.960
and now I'm going to wash a T-shirt.

167
00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.600
I really

168
00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.940
don't like the material,

169
00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:11.500
so

170
00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.220
I won't buy them anymore.

171
00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.540
They look amazing,

172
00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.340
that's true,

173
00:13:15.340 --> 00:13:16.920
as for that,

174
00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:17.860
everything's great here,

175
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.120
and they look good in photos,

176
00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:19.880
and fit well,

177
00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:20.620
accentuate the figure,

178
00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.880
but what a nightmare...

179
00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.440
Actually I can't show you this,

180
00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:30.780
because I forgot to take off

181
00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.900
the face mask,

182
00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.000
which is really great,

183
00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:33.920
yesterday I didn't even

184
00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.320
apply makeup,

185
00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:36.980
my skin was that beautiful,

186
00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.640
but I'll film it for you

187
00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.180
when I find this mask

188
00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:40.580
again,

189
00:13:40.580 --> 00:13:41.080
because,

190
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.420
when I went

191
00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.460
to buy it now,

192
00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.540
it was, unfortunately, not there,

193
00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:50.060
so I'll order it from the "Lilly" website,

194
00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:51.480
and show you

195
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:52.040
which one I mean,

196
00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.000
because it really

197
00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.320
restores the skin,

198
00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:55.460
it's crazy.

199
00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.420
I've already tired you out,

200
00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.080
see you

201
00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:00.860
another time,

202
00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:01.880
in another place.

203
00:14:22.490 --> 00:14:23.210
Little horse,

204
00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.590
where are you, little horse?

205
00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:25.590
Is this horse tied up?

206
00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:26.750
Beautiful.

207
00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:56.210
And the last stop

208
00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.730
on our trip —

209
00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.490
the Krupaja spring.

210
00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:00.550
We are

211
00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:01.730
now at the parking lot.

212
00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:03.890
200 dinars

213
00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:04.850
is the parking fee,

214
00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:05.870
and, if you have

215
00:15:05.870 --> 00:15:07.330
small children,

216
00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:08.530
they won't charge you

217
00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:09.170
anything.

218
00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:10.870
But people park en masse

219
00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:12.370
wherever they like,

220
00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.030
so there's

221
00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:14.850
a terrible crowd here.

222
00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:17.230
Honestly, there are really a lot of people,

223
00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:18.350
many more than

224
00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.450
at the waterfall

225
00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.610
where we were yesterday.

226
00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.750
Today is Sunday,

227
00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:23.570
so I suppose

228
00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:24.610
it's because of that.

229
00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.750
Now we'll

230
00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.050
walk

231
00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.270
to

232
00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:30.510
the spring itself,

233
00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:32.750
and after that

234
00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.810
we're driving on,

235
00:15:33.810 --> 00:15:34.270
because

236
00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.190
we won't sit

237
00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:35.710
in the restaurant,

238
00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:36.550
and, I suppose,

239
00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:37.390
there's a terrible

240
00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:37.990
crowd there.

241
00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:38.630
And the question is

242
00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:39.330
whether we'll be able to

243
00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:39.990
approach

244
00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.670
the Krupaja spring,

245
00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.090
considering

246
00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:42.590
there's really

247
00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:43.770
a ton of people here.

248
00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.450
Literally like

249
00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:49.010
a fair.

250
00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.230
The little one is slathered with cream

251
00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:55.170
and ready

252
00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:57.210
for action.

253
00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:05.210
We've gotten somewhere around halfway.

254
00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.290
This is a trail,

255
00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:08.870
and down below,

256
00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:09.870
you hear,

257
00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:10.910
a huge crowd.

258
00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:12.770
The crowd is because there's a restaurant here

259
00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:13.890
with a natural

260
00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:14.510
pool,

261
00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:17.550
where water flows

262
00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:18.230
from the spring,

263
00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:19.490
and there it sort of warms up,

264
00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:20.790
so the temperature is pleasant

265
00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.430
for swimming.

266
00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.230
Very many people,

267
00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:24.430
and mostly children

268
00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:24.990
are swimming,

269
00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:26.210
so you can come

270
00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:31.310
just for that.

271
00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:34.970
There are many people.

272
00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.630
When we were here

273
00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:38.090
a couple of years ago,

274
00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:39.850
there was literally nobody,

275
00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:41.090
nobody at all.

276
00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:42.230
And this isn't nice,

277
00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.050
really not nice.

278
00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:43.930
You can't leave it

279
00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:44.490
like this.

280
00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.530
That is, you should

281
00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.250
take your trash

282
00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:48.050
with you.

283
00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.520
In any case I

284
00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.060
recommend

285
00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.460
coming here

286
00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:07.620
on a weekday,

287
00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:09.120
that is, avoid

288
00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.020
Friday, Saturday, Sunday,

289
00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:10.700
because there really is

290
00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:11.360
a big crowd here.

291
00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:13.500
I don't know whether you'll be able

292
00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:13.980
to see and

293
00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:14.700
photograph anything,

294
00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:15.880
because there really,

295
00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:16.480
really are many people here.

296
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.160
We arrived at the Manasija monastery.

297
00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.820
Unlike the Krupaja spring,

298
00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.000
there isn't such a big crowd here,

299
00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.860
mostly families with children,

300
00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:24.260
so

301
00:17:24.260 --> 00:17:25.920
you can drive in here.

302
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.320
It's really very beautiful here.

303
00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.180
Fortress walls all around.

304
00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:33.830
You can't take photos in the monastery,

305
00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:34.310
so

306
00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:35.530
we'll go in,

307
00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.490
but, of course, we'll respect that

308
00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.550
and won't snap photos.

309
00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.950
Also you can't enter the monastery

310
00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:43.250
in

311
00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:44.790
shorts,

312
00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:45.870
a tank top,

313
00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:46.550
flip-flops,

314
00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:48.370
so we stick to that,

315
00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:49.430
which I recommend to you too.

316
00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.070
Not everyone here sticks to it.

317
00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.240
What I must tell you —

318
00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:02.760
is that

319
00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.660
I saw very many people

320
00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.580
who don't observe

321
00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:06.660
the most elementary

322
00:18:06.660 --> 00:18:08.040
monastery rules.

323
00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:12.640
Our churches

324
00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.580
don't require women

325
00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:15.900
to cover their heads,

326
00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.740
but what

327
00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:18.960
would be good —

328
00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:20.280
is to observe at least this,

329
00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.500
to come in trousers

330
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:25.360
and with something long below,

331
00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.760
and, of course, to cover the shoulders.

332
00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:28.000
That would be very good,

333
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:28.900
because I know that

334
00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:30.280
most of you observe

335
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.640
all the rules

336
00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:33.200
when you go on trips

337
00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.040
abroad,

338
00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.080
so it would be fine

339
00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.100
to observe them here too.

340
00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.500
Today is Monday,

341
00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:40.180
the last day

342
00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.160
at the Resava ethno village,

343
00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.840
which means

344
00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.700
we're driving home.

345
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:49.400
This is one of those places

346
00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.060
that I would

347
00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.120
recommend wholeheartedly

348
00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:51.660
that you visit.

349
00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.940
There are many reasons.

350
00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:55.920
Let's begin:

351
00:18:55.920 --> 00:18:58.220
first, there are animals everywhere

352
00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:58.840
around,

353
00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.740
horses, donkeys, dogs,

354
00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.120
very interesting,

355
00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.060
they all roam freely,

356
00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.300
at any time you can

357
00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:04.960
approach them,

358
00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:05.900
pet them,

359
00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.200
I really like that.

360
00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.060
The food here

361
00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.080
is very good,

362
00:19:12.220 --> 00:19:13.980
real, genuine

363
00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:15.040
home cooking.

364
00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:17.380
We, for example,

365
00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.100
just

366
00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:18.940
ate nonstop here

367
00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:19.520
pancakes,

368
00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:20.480
because the pancakes here

369
00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:21.960
are thicker,

370
00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:22.800
that is, not like

371
00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.480
when I make them

372
00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:25.460
at home,

373
00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:26.380
but like

374
00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.200
homestyle, as they say.

375
00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:29.940
There are options,

376
00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.560
of course, "Nutella," "Eurocrem," "Plazma,"

377
00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:32.680
but there's also an option

378
00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.320
with homemade jam

379
00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:34.960
made from apricots

380
00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:35.540
and from plums.

381
00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.720
They're very tasty.

382
00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:38.980
The grilled meat here

383
00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:39.640
is very good.

384
00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:42.140
The lodging we took —

385
00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.140
we took an apartment.

386
00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:44.700
The apartment is

387
00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.800
so big,

388
00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:48.800
I have a feeling

389
00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:49.240
that, basically,

390
00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:50.120
the whole floor is ours.

391
00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.600
It's very big,

392
00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:52.420
everything's very spacious,

393
00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.460
there's something like a small kitchen,

394
00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:55.040
which came in handy for us

395
00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.020
because of the bottle

396
00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:56.800
and all that.

397
00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.680
A big bed,

398
00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:01.000
two more extra beds,

399
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:01.560
that is, it's literally

400
00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:02.280
for 4 people,

401
00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:02.920
easily.

402
00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.000
We had room to set up

403
00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:06.040
the portable crib

404
00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:07.280
that we brought along.

405
00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.700
A very high ceiling,

406
00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:10.160
and overall

407
00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.880
a really big space,

408
00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.600
also decorated in ethno style.

409
00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:14.560
Lots of room

410
00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:15.320
to walk around.

411
00:20:15.320 --> 00:20:17.620
And the most important thing for me,

412
00:20:17.620 --> 00:20:19.200
with which I wanted to end

413
00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:19.880
this trip —

414
00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:20.200
is

415
00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.160
that it be out of town,

416
00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.320
I really wanted it to be

417
00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.240
something very, very

418
00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:29.140
far from the city.

419
00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.300
Around here there's

420
00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:30.980
literally nothing,

421
00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:32.020
except this estate,

422
00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:32.480
so

423
00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.280
I like it very, very much.

424
00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:35.560
Now we'll show

425
00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:36.680
what it looks like,

426
00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:37.620
what I was talking about.

427
00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:38.600
We're going to breakfast,

428
00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:39.380
after that

429
00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.320
we'll film a few things

430
00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.900
and slowly head home.

431
00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:42.800
We're finishing this tour,

432
00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:43.100
or rather,

433
00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.700
the tour ended yesterday.

434
00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:47.980
We finished the project

435
00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.000
"Travel Around Serbia"

436
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.260
with EKO Srbija

437
00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:52.180
and took one extra day

438
00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:52.760
to stay,

439
00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:53.560
rest a bit,

440
00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:56.300
to let the impressions settle a bit,

441
00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:59.100
to play a little more

442
00:20:59.100 --> 00:20:59.820
with the horses,

443
00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.700
because Nadja likes them.

444
00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.640
I said that this is

445
00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:02.560
one big toy

446
00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:03.120
just for her,

447
00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.500
so she was thrilled.

448
00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:08.540
All right, let's go have breakfast.

449
00:21:12.990 --> 00:21:13.950
Our breakfast

450
00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:15.650
is served.

451
00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:17.950
We have pancakes,

452
00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:19.850
a little coffee,

453
00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:24.090
eggs.

454
00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:30.230
In principle,

455
00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:31.190
that's it.

456
00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:33.890
Organic food,

457
00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.230
everything has a very pleasant and rich flavor.

458
00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:39.790
And the jam is very good.

459
00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:02.080
I volunteered to help them round up the horses.

460
00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:03.420
By the time I got there,

461
00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:04.860
the horses had already gone in.

462
00:23:27.820 --> 00:23:29.800
But, folks, how well you sleep here!

463
00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:34.240
Now it's really time to check out. Check-out here is until twelve.

464
00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:35.960
We've already checked out,

465
00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:38.280
and yet we stayed sitting here,

466
00:23:38.280 --> 00:23:39.960
and we don't want to go home.

467
00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:41.960
We rested so well, folks,

468
00:23:42.740 --> 00:23:44.940
although we worked a lot, we really rested.

469
00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:46.540
We had time for everything,

470
00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:49.260
everything went unhurried,

471
00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:50.600
there was no rush at all,

472
00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:51.880
and we liked that very much.

473
00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.980
This is actually the first ethno village we've visited.

474
00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:58.300
I hope that

475
00:23:58.300 --> 00:23:59.420
most are in the same spirit,

476
00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:01.500
because we really plan to visit a few more,

477
00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:02.720
we've already looked a bit on Booking,

478
00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:04.200
where that might be,

479
00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:06.340
and overall we really like the concept and the idea,

480
00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:08.400
so here we are in ethnotourism.

481
00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:09.900
Thank you very much for watching this vlog,

482
00:24:09.900 --> 00:24:11.440
see you soon in the next one.

483
00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:13.840
Be sure to write to me below how well you can hear and see me

484
00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.140
throughout this whole vlog,

485
00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:17.120
because everything was filmed on one device,

486
00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:19.160
so it's very important for me to know how we sound.

487
00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:20.420
And that's all.

488
00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:22.060
See you, folks, in the next vlog.

489
00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:22.400
Bye.